    "result_text": "Full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `contactPreference` field on the owner response \u2014 `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE` \u2014 following the project's existing derived-field pattern (the same shape as `membershipLevel` and `locality`):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema, so `OwnerDto` is generated with the field and its getter/setter.\n\n2. **`util/ContactPreference.java`** \u2014 new util with `preferenceOf(Owner)` returning `\"EMAIL\"` when `owner.getEmail()` is non-null and non-empty, else `\"PHONE\"` (mirrors how `MembershipLevel.levelOf` inspects the email).\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 imported the util and added `@Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\", expression = \"java(ContactPreference.preferenceOf(owner))\")` so every `toOwnerDto` mapping populates it.\n\nI deliberately kept the schema field a plain `string` (values documented in the description) rather than an inline `enum`, because the project has no other enums and the `spring` generator would have produced a nested `ContactPreferenceEnum` type whose setter wouldn't accept the mapper's `String` expression.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest.corePhoneWhenNoEmail` and `functionalityEmailWhenPresent` both pass, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures.",
